{"answer": "Yes, master mode is supported. The I2C module supports multi-master mode, although there are specific functional restrictions regarding master collisions and hold times for the start condition [S1]. Additionally, features such as configurable repeated start in master mode are supported [S3]. The operation details, including states for master transmitting and receiving, are described in the documentation [S2].", "base_url": "http://106.106.152.161:4000/v1", "candidate_k": 12, "chunks": "data/chunks_i2c_ch34_v2.jsonl", "collection": "I2C_Ch34_v2", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "code", "question": "Is the master mode supported?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 5, "bm25_score": 6.492737491167265, "chunk_index": 15, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1383, "page_start": 1383, "score": -0.031009615384615385, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 4}, {"bm25_rank": 10, "bm25_score": 4.640352444097358, "chunk_index": 39, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1395, "page_start": 1395, "score": -0.030679156908665108, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 8, "bm25_score": 5.453245844145233, "chunk_index": 1, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1375, "page_start": 1375, "score": -0.02919863597612958, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 9}, {"bm25_rank": 12, "bm25_score": 4.5927812487707005, "chunk_index": 32, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1392, "page_start": 1392, "score": -0.028814262023217248, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 7}, {"bm25_rank": 11, "bm25_score": 4.600909517088878, "chunk_index": 40, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1395, "page_start": 1395, "score": -0.028169014084507043, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 11}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T14:03:09.611612+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "The supported data transfer rates for the I2C module are as follows [S2][S4]:\n\n*   **Standard mode:** Up to 100 kbit/s (range: 20 kbit/s - 100 kbit/s) [S2][S4].\n*   **Fast mode:** Up to 400 kbit/s (range: 100 kbit/s - 400 kbit/s) [S2][S4].\n*   **High-speed mode:** Up to 3.4 Mbit/s (range: 500 kbit/s - 3.4 Mbit/s) [S2][S4][S5].", "base_url": "http://106.106.152.161:4000/v1", "candidate_k": 12, "chunks": "data/chunks_i2c_ch34_v2.jsonl", "collection": "I2C_Ch34_v2", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "code", "question": "What are the supported data transfer rates?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 11, "bm25_score": 6.395750872689508, "chunk_index": 12, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1381, "page_start": 1381, "score": -0.03021353930031804, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 9.327623908332825, "chunk_index": 4, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1377, "page_start": 1377, "score": -0.029957522915269395, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 11}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 7, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1378, "page_start": 1378, "score": -0.01639344262295082, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 9.681144314117352, "chunk_index": 0, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1375, "page_start": 1375, "score": -0.01639344262295082, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": null}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 9.328608317145825, "chunk_index": 13, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1382, "page_start": 1382, "score": -0.016129032258064516, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": null}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T14:03:11.883077+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "The start and stop conditions are realized through specific transitions on the SDA line while the SCL line remains high:\n\n*   **Start Condition:** Indicated by a high-to-low transition on the SDA line while SCL is high [S1][S2].\n*   **Stop Condition:** Defined by a low-to-high transition on the SDA line while SCL is high [S1][S2].", "base_url": "http://106.106.152.161:4000/v1", "candidate_k": 12, "chunks": "data/chunks_i2c_ch34_v2.jsonl", "collection": "I2C_Ch34_v2", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "code", "question": "How are the start and stop conditions realized?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 9.817270593382784, "chunk_index": 5, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1377, "page_start": 1377, "score": -0.03252247488101534, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 10.133385726354117, "chunk_index": 4, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1377, "page_start": 1377, "score": -0.031099324975891997, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 8}, {"bm25_rank": 4, "bm25_score": 7.702876293143401, "chunk_index": 17, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1384, "page_start": 1384, "score": -0.029910714285714284, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 10}, {"bm25_rank": 5, "bm25_score": 7.446975068091659, "chunk_index": 6, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1378, "page_start": 1378, "score": -0.029877369007803793, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 9}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 98, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1436, "page_start": 1436, "score": -0.016129032258064516, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 2}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T14:03:13.243729+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "To perform 10-bit slave addressing in I2C, the following procedure is used:\n\n1.  **First Address Byte (Preamble):** The master transmits a preamble address with the bit pattern `11110XX` followed by the `RnW` bit set to `0`. The `XX` bits represent the two most significant bits of the 10-bit slave address [S1]. This specific bit combination is reserved for the 10-bit addressing mode [S3][S4].\n2.  **Acknowledge:** At least one slave matching the 10-bit address must acknowledge this first byte [S1].\n3.  **Second Address Byte:** The master transmits a second address byte containing the eight least significant bits of the 10-bit address [S1].\n4.  **Final Acknowledge:** Only the slave whose combined 10-bit address matches the transmitted bits acknowledges the second byte [S1].\n5.  **Data Transmission:** Data packages can then be transmitted to the addressed slave until a stop or restart condition occurs [S1].\n\nFor read operations, a restart condition is required. The master first transmits the 10-bit address (preamble with `RnW=0` followed by the second address byte). After a restart condition, the master sends the preamble address `11110XX` again, but this time with `RnW=1`, and then receives the data [S1].", "base_url": "http://106.106.152.161:4000/v1", "candidate_k": 12, "chunks": "data/chunks_i2c_ch34_v2.jsonl", "collection": "I2C_Ch34_v2", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "code", "question": "How to do the 10-bit slave addressing?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 11.904175928139253, "chunk_index": 11, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1381, "page_start": 1381, "score": -0.03278688524590164, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 10.934435263906781, "chunk_index": 12, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1381, "page_start": 1381, "score": -0.03200204813108039, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 3}, {"bm25_rank": 4, "bm25_score": 9.56764171198476, "chunk_index": 7, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1378, "page_start": 1378, "score": -0.030776515151515152, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 6}, {"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 9.747015831591453, "chunk_index": 6, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1378, "page_start": 1378, "score": -0.03036576949620428, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 9}, {"bm25_rank": 5, "bm25_score": 9.12609461750722, "chunk_index": 95, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1435, "page_start": 1435, "score": -0.030090497737556562, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 8}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T14:03:17.503443+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "Based on the provided context, the **CLC1** register is used to select operational modes related to clock control, specifically:\n\n*   **Disabled Mode:** Selected by setting the `DISR` bit in the CLC1 register (`CLC1.DISR = 1`) [S5].\n*   **OCDS Suspend Mode:** Selected by setting the `SPEN` bit in the CLC1 register (`CLC1.SPEN = 1`) [S3, S5].\n\nAdditionally, within the OCDS Suspend mode, specific disable features are selectable via the `FSOE` bit in the **CLC1** register [S3, S5].\n\nFor general peripheral operation, the document also distinguishes between **Configuration Mode** and **Run Mode**, which are selected by the state of the `RUN` bit (though the specific register name containing the `RUN` bit is not explicitly defined in the text, only the bit name and mode conditions are provided) [S1].", "base_url": "http://106.106.152.161:4000/v1", "candidate_k": 12, "chunks": "data/chunks_i2c_ch34_v2.jsonl", "collection": "I2C_Ch34_v2", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "code", "question": "Which register is used to select the operational mode?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 8, "bm25_score": 9.250347152700863, "chunk_index": 87, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1429, "page_start": 1429, "score": -0.031099324975891997, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 12.030666016636328, "chunk_index": 81, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1425, "page_start": 1425, "score": -0.01639344262295082, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": null}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 71, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1417, "page_start": 1417, "score": -0.016129032258064516, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 10.572816367063524, "chunk_index": 18, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1385, "page_start": 1385, "score": -0.016129032258064516, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": null}, {"bm25