{"answer": "Based on the provided context, the **MRPS** bit-field (maximum receive packet size) in the **MRPSCTRL** register is used to trigger data transmission. Specifically, writing to the MRPS bit-field generates an **MRPS_start** trigger to the I2C kernel to initiate a reception when the peripheral is in master-receiver mode [S5].\n\nAdditionally, writing to the **TPSCTRL** register can initiate a transmission when the interrupt routine proceeds upon entering a specific state, provided the bus status and RnW bits identify the slave-transmitter mode [S2].", "base_url": "http://106.106.152.161:4000/v1", "candidate_k": 12, "chunks": "data/chunks_i2c_ch34_v2.jsonl", "collection": "I2C_Ch34_v2", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "code", "question": "Which bit is used to trigger the data transmission?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 5, "bm25_score": 11.381459392449157, "chunk_index": 43, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1396, "page_start": 1396, "score": -0.031009615384615385, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 4}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 12.229244110505617, "chunk_index": 30, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1392, "page_start": 1392, "score": -0.030621785881252923, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 9}, {"bm25_rank": 12, "bm25_score": 10.318376138455251, "chunk_index": 67, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1414, "page_start": 1414, "score": -0.02904040404040404, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 6}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 7, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1378, "page_start": 1378, "score": -0.01639344262295082, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 16.655416991953707, "chunk_index": 57, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1407, "page_start": 1407, "score": -0.01639344262295082, "source": "I2C Ch34", "vector_rank": null}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T14:03:22.309924+00:00", "token_para